# vitagl-0007: hardening from a code review.
# - gxm.c: init_depth_stencil_buffer returns GLboolean and, when storage is missing, frees the half that
#   succeeded and initializes nothing; scene_reset then opens no scene (as 0006 does for a missing target)
#   and keeps the retry armed. mark_as_dirty drops NULL (the collector stops at the first NULL entry).
#   Also #error unless built with SINGLE_THREADED_GC=1: the async collector rotates the purge indices
#   unsynchronised with the render thread (build-vitagl.sh passes the knob).
# - custom_shaders.c: unserialize_shader validates every offset, a 64-byte minimum GXP header (before
#   sceGxmProgramCheck, which runs on an aligned private copy), the parameter table and matrix indices;
#   checks the allocations and sceGxmShaderPatcherRegisterProgram; leaves the shader untouched on failure
#   (s->size is the source length); returns OK/CORRUPT/RESOURCE so only CORRUPT deletes a cache file.
#   load_cached_shader (one reader for glCompileShader/glLinkProgram) reads fully, retries the shipped
#   fallback after a bad primary, and never deletes on OOM. glShaderBinary reports errors;
#   glGetProgramiv/glGetProgramInfoLog validate the handle and a failed link's NULL vertex program.
# - buffers.c: glGenBuffers is all-or-nothing on OOM (was a NULL dereference).
# - gpu_utils.c/textures.c: cube, compressed-cube, paletted and planar (re)specification allocate before
#   they free, never mark a texture name TEX_UNUSED while its owner holds it, free a half-made pair, and
#   the compressed paths return GLboolean so callers skip the descriptor patch-back after a refusal;
#   compressed staging failure falls back to the CPU swizzle. The compressed cube checked base + offset.
# - mem_utils.c: a pool whose memblock failed reports size 0 (vglMemTotal), not its requested size.
